  "id": "COMPOUND:30099 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Polygonatoside A is implicated in the interaction with SK-VLB through a multi-step pathway involving the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one, which both direct their targets to SK-VLB. The shared involvement of the sialyltransferase in these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which Polygonatoside A may influence SK-VLB through this enzyme. The evidence points to a dependency on the sialyltransferase as a critical node in the interaction, with multiple compounds targeting the same enzyme and ultimately leading to SK-VLB. This indicates that the relationship between Polygonatoside A and SK-VLB is likely mediated through this enzyme, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
